     "body": "<p><em>When committing a long running Fedora transaction, in which the time needed to perform the commit is long (due to a large total size of files of many gigabytes and a large numbers of files for example), the database connections needs to stay open for a long time without any activity because moving all those files from OCFL staging directory to the OCFL root (committing the OCFL persistent storage session,</em> <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/a2ec2ac5b273670c421b74df1ad9174b3289f663/fcrepo-kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/impl/TransactionImpl.java#L361\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\"><ins><em>fcrepo-kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/impl/TransactionImpl.java#L361</em></ins></a><em>) can take a considerable amount of time.</em></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3970?src=confmacro\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3970?src=confmacro</a> </p>",
     "created": "03/Jul/25 12:36 PM",
